§ `Section 4: when the enactment comes into force`

#ASSERT (`section 4 — when the enactment comes into force` (`An enactment` WITH `its kind` IS `an Act`, `the day it was passed or made` IS (YMD 2026 3 10), `what it says about coming into force` IS `no provision`))'s `the day` EQUALS (YMD 2026 3 10)
#ASSERT (`section 4 — when the enactment comes into force` (`An enactment` WITH `its kind` IS `an Act`, `the day it was passed or made` IS (YMD 2026 3 10), `what it says about coming into force` IS `no provision`))'s `the moment within the day` EQUALS `the beginning of the day`
#ASSERT (`section 4 — when the enactment comes into force` (`An enactment` WITH `its kind` IS `an Act`, `the day it was passed or made` IS (YMD 2026 3 10), `what it says about coming into force` IS (`a particular day` WITH `that day` IS (YMD 2026 4 1))))'s `the day` EQUALS (YMD 2026 4 1)
#ASSERT (`section 4 — when the enactment comes into force` (`An enactment` WITH `its kind` IS `an Act`, `the day it was passed or made` IS (YMD 2026 3 10), `what it says about coming into force` IS (`a particular day` WITH `that day` IS (YMD 2026 4 1))))'s `the moment within the day` EQUALS `the beginning of the day`
#ASSERT (`section 4 — when the enactment comes into force` (`An enactment` WITH `its kind` IS `an Act`, `the day it was passed or made` IS (YMD 2026 3 10), `what it says about coming into force` IS (`a day to be fixed later` WITH `the day once fixed` IS (JUST (YMD 2026 6 1)))))'s `the day` EQUALS (YMD 2026 6 1)
#ASSERT REFUSED `section 4 — when the enactment comes into force` (`An enactment` WITH `its kind` IS `an Act`, `the day it was passed or made` IS (YMD 1880 3 10), `what it says about coming into force` IS `no provision`) BECAUSE "section 4 does not apply to an enactment passed or made in or before 1889, and the Interpretation Act 1978 has no other rule on its coming into force"
#ASSERT REFUSED `section 4 — when the enactment comes into force` (`An enactment` WITH `its kind` IS `an Act`, `the day it was passed or made` IS (YMD 2026 3 10), `what it says about coming into force` IS (`a day to be fixed later` WITH `the day once fixed` IS NOTHING)) BECAUSE "the enactment provides for a day to be fixed later and none is fixed yet, so neither limb of section 4 gives a day"
